From a7d09236861dd11fac2b88e4c3472eeec0a895a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:24:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] block 12: k-quant-boosts Q4_K/Q5_K VDR=4 decode,
 mmq scale hoist, MoE whitelist

Q4_K/Q5_K were the remaining k-quants on mainline mmvq/mmap paths. This
block applies the block-04/09 optimizations to them:

- VDR=4 mmvq decode kernels (32 elements/thread, shared scale/d8 loads):
  decode n=1 improves -13%..-18% (q4_K) and -8%..-15% (q5_K) on the
  Qwen3.6-27B shapes; verify batch n=2..8 -2%..-13%. Real-model
  (Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_XL, mixed Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q8_0): decode +5.5-5.7%.
- mmq prefill scale-load hoist in vec_dot_q8_1_q8_1_mma (block-04 style):
  q4_K n=16 prefill -4.6%.
- RDNA4 MoE mmid whitelist Q4_K 4->7 (n=5/6/7 per expert -22%..-28%);
  Q5_K stays at 5 (wash vs mmq, verified against a CUDA-graph artifact).
- perf harness: Q4_K/Q5_K decode + prefill rows, MUL_MAT_ID bs=5/6/7.

Assisted-by: pi
